hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1142","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan bin Shaqiq told us, Abu Hamza told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever memorizes these prescribed prayers will not be recorded as one of the heedless, and whoever recites them in One hundred nights, that is, it was not recorded from the heedless, or it was written from the obedient ones.” And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best speech is four: Glory be to God, praise be to God, there is no god but God, and God is great.”"
